WEBVTT

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:16.490
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:34.120
Animal Field Baseball Part 1!

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:42.740
Grass, huh?

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:45.350
Grass is great, isn't it?

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:46.760
What?

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:49.560
Bamboo grass is much better 
than regular grass.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:50.770
Welcome.

00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:52.380
We're not talking about eating it.

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:54.320
We're talking about field baseball.

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:55.590
Field baseball?

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:59.620
We all eat grass while 
playing baseball.

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:02.050
No, we don't.

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:05.910
The café team will 
be playing baseball

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:07.390
against Mr. Grizzly's team soon.

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:13.070
Grizzly gave us an invitation.

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:15.940
An invitation <i>(shoutaijou)</i>?

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:18.900
That would be Nagoya 
Castle <i>(Nagoya jou)</i>.

00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:22.150
That would be a 
receptionist <i>(uketsukejou)</i>.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:25.290
Happy New Year! 
-Polar Bear

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:25.290
That would be a New Year's 
card <i>(nengajou)</i>.

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:28.650
An invitation, Polar Bear.

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:30.580
Yes, it's right here.

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:34.590
Declaration of Battle 
-Grizzly

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:32.780
See?

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:38.050
I don't think that's 
what you think it is.

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:42.040
<i>I hereby challenge you to a duel</i>

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:43.680
<i>at the petting zoo baseball field.</i>

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:46.140
<i>Burn it up! Burn it up!</i>

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:49.960
Wow, so you're having a duel.

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:52.040
We're talking about a baseball game.

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:55.900
Game Day

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:09.580
Burn it up, Wild Animals!

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:11.960
Burn it up, burn it up!

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:13.530
Burn it up, burn it up!

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:16.240
They're so wild and cool!

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:18.990
It's like a wild kingdom.

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:22.390
The Polar Bears are 
going to take it easy.

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:24.240
Okay.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:33.840
I wonder what I should do if 
I get scouted to the pros.

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:35.460
You won't need to worry about that.

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:36.800
More importantly, Panda,

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:38.400
you're playing right 
field, aren't you?

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:42.740
Lesser Panda switched with me.

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:43.950
What?

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:48.130
Are you sure you're okay with playing 
right field, Lesser Panda?

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:48.830
Yes.

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:53.390
Panda is the sunflower 
of the animal world.

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:57.000
I'm an evening primrose 
that blooms quietly.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:59.460
R-Really?

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:01.780
Let's bring it in!

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:08.060
I wanted to clean my fan today

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:11.250
since I finally had a day off.

00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:14.330
We're counting on you, Mr. Handa.

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:16.820
Play ball!

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:22.150
You seem rather into it, Mr. Handa.

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:26.030
Them vegetarians ain't got nothin'!

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:29.550
Show 'em what us carnivores are made of!

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:30.910
Leave it to me.

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:38.630
What?!

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:44.040
You won't be able to hit my pitches.

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:46.170
No, Panda!

00:04:46.170 --> 00:04:46.840
Huh?

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.600
You have to throw towards the batter!

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:53.300
But if I throw it that way, 
he'll hit the ball.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:56.300
Well that's what baseball is...

00:04:56.850 --> 00:04:57.940
Got it!

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:00.580
So it's okay if they hit the ball?

00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:03.520
Throw it so they won't hit it.

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:06.370
This is complicated.

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:09.120
Forget it. You can step aside.

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:13.000
Th-Then I can...

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:15.300
I'll pitch.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:15.940
Wha?

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:21.600
I'll stun them with my amazing pitch,
 the South Pole Blizzard.

00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:35.360
Burn it up! Burn it up!

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:37.600
My ball's on fire!

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:40.770
Wild Animals

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:40.770
We just got four home runs in a row!

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:43.670
Nice batting, Boss.

00:05:43.670 --> 00:05:47.060
All right, let's keep it up!

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:50.290
Nice pitching, Mr. Penguin!

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:53.830
At this rate, we're doomed.

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:55.630
Please hurry and throw 
the amazing pitch,

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:57.210
the South Pole Blizzard!

00:05:59.890 --> 00:06:04.300
You know, I'm much better at 
water polo than baseball.

00:06:05.070 --> 00:06:07.220
We're switching pitchers.

00:06:11.980 --> 00:06:14.010
Let's play a good game.

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:17.300
Well, isn't he fancy.

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:19.770
Get wild and hit it out of the park!

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:22.750
I'm going to continue 
with another home run.

00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:35.940
Strike!

00:06:37.270 --> 00:06:38.610
A change up?

00:06:39.140 --> 00:06:40.680
How'd he throw that?

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:44.880
Strike! Batter out!

00:06:47.370 --> 00:06:49.680
Strike! Batter out!

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:54.180
Strike! Batter out!

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:56.680
Incredible...

00:06:57.250 --> 00:06:59.340
He's a tiny giant.

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:04.440
Bottom of the 1st Inning

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:06.940
Wild Animals

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:06.940
Polar Bears

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:09.700
Do your best, Mr. Penguin!

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:16.240
Behold! Penguin's Lake!

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:24.640
What?

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:30.880
Well, that's an easy out!

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:35.800
Safe!

00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:38.150
Nice play!

00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:40.390
You're amazing, Mr. Penguin!

00:07:42.650 --> 00:07:44.940
Masaki!

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:52.000
<i>Throw it to the inside corner 
and scare the crap out of him.</i>

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:57.360
Ball!

00:07:58.530 --> 00:08:00.750
<i>I thought he'd freak out 
and swing at it.</i>

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:02.710
<i>He didn't even flinch!</i>

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:05.420
Ball!

00:08:07.240 --> 00:08:07.750
Ball!

00:08:08.430 --> 00:08:10.700
Ball! Four balls!

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:14.500
That was ball four, Panda.

00:08:14.950 --> 00:08:16.350
Take your base.

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:21.600
He's asleep!

00:08:24.610 --> 00:08:28.150
Mr. Penguin! I did it!

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:29.690
See!

00:08:29.010 --> 00:08:30.660
Well, he got on base, 
so I guess it's okay.

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:31.360
I'm awesome!

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:35.950
This is our chance to tie up the game.

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:38.590
Hit a home run!

00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:45.910
Ramen with pork!

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:47.960
Damn it!

00:08:48.470 --> 00:08:49.630
There it goes!

00:08:56.950 --> 00:08:58.060
Nice catch!

00:08:58.060 --> 00:08:58.990
Tagged up!

00:08:58.990 --> 00:08:59.560
What?!

00:09:04.670 --> 00:09:05.600
Safe!

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:07.360
Yay!

00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:09.650
Nice play, Mr. Penguin!

00:09:09.670 --> 00:09:11.150
Wild Animals

00:09:09.670 --> 00:09:11.150
Polar Bears

00:09:11.190 --> 00:09:13.400
Top of the 2nd Inning

00:09:17.960 --> 00:09:19.120
Left field!

00:09:20.550 --> 00:09:21.370
Huh?

00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:26.760
Stop eating grass during the game!

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:28.540
But it's delicious.

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:31.590
Why don't you have some 
too, Mr. Penguin?

00:09:32.190 --> 00:09:35.100
Could you eat after the game?

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:37.590
Bottom of the 3rd Inning

00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:45.640
This time it's a home run for sure!

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:54.720
Top of the 5th Inning

00:09:58.930 --> 00:09:59.990
Left field!

00:10:02.420 --> 00:10:05.560
Hey! I told you to eat later!

00:10:06.310 --> 00:10:08.430
But I'm having dessert.

00:10:08.430 --> 00:10:10.670
Have your dessert later, too!

00:10:11.950 --> 00:10:13.150
Strike!

00:10:15.770 --> 00:10:16.800
He's asleep?!

00:10:23.460 --> 00:10:24.200
Huh?

00:10:28.150 --> 00:10:31.100
You need to hold off on eating, too, Anteater!

00:10:35.220 --> 00:10:38.370
Come on! Eat dessert later!

00:10:39.300 --> 00:10:41.740
Bottom of the 7th Inning

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:44.790
Wild Animals

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:44.790
Polar Bears

00:10:48.970 --> 00:10:53.290
Polar Bear! We can still win
 with a grand slam!

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:56.670
I don't think so!

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:59.010
They have two outs! Just one more out!

00:10:59.440 --> 00:11:01.320
I hope you get a home run!

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:03.100
Make it a walk-off home run!

00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:05.080
Hold it!

00:11:07.920 --> 00:11:09.440
We're changing pitchers.

00:11:10.660 --> 00:11:12.900
Are they bringing out 
their secret weapon?

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:15.240
It's up to you, Boss.

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:23.530
Polar Bear.

00:11:25.720 --> 00:11:28.870
I'll strike you out with 
my flaming straight ball.

00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:35.100
What?

00:11:35.100 --> 00:11:36.550
A called shot?

00:11:57.090 --> 00:12:01.900
To Be Continued in Part 2!

00:11:57.090 --> 00:12:01.900
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:09.910
What's Jacu coffee!?

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:11.870
What's...  Jacu coffee?!

00:12:14.890 --> 00:12:16.040
<i>My name's Masaki.</i>

00:12:17.050 --> 00:12:19.630
<i>I'm currently learning 
how to roast coffee</i>

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:22.250
<i>under my mentor, Mr. Tree Kangaroo.</i>

00:12:24.370 --> 00:12:26.000
Masaki, did you know?

00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:27.640
This is a coffee cherry.

00:12:28.020 --> 00:12:29.890
Huh? It's red.

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:30.950
Why?

00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:33.660
Red means that it's completely ripe.

00:12:34.070 --> 00:12:36.440
So when it's ripe, it looks like this?

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:40.940
The seed within the red 
cherry is the coffee bean.

00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:45.200
There are two seeds within the cherry.

00:12:45.590 --> 00:12:46.680
What?!

00:12:46.680 --> 00:12:48.870
So a coffee bean is a seed?

00:12:49.610 --> 00:12:52.140
I wonder if this kid will make it...

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:57.710
That bird sure comes by a lot.

00:12:57.710 --> 00:12:59.170
That's Mr. Jacu. {Not sure if it's Mr. or Ms...}

00:12:59.740 --> 00:13:02.480
Oh, so his name is Jacu.

00:13:03.610 --> 00:13:05.130
Don't be so rude.

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:07.090
Call him "Mr. Jacu."

00:13:07.090 --> 00:13:08.680
Why?

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:10.980
He's a very important client.

00:13:10.980 --> 00:13:12.280
Mind your manners!

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:24.700
I've poured us some coffee, 
so let's take a break!

00:13:25.260 --> 00:13:27.000
Thanks for the coffee!

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:32.400
This tastes different than usual.

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:35.250
My, you're sharper than you look.

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:37.390
Are the beans from somewhere else?

00:13:37.390 --> 00:13:40.280
No, it's just roasted differently.

00:13:40.700 --> 00:13:42.630
It tastes completely different.

00:13:43.030 --> 00:13:44.940
Of course!

00:13:44.940 --> 00:13:47.680
The taste of coffee is 
determined by the roast!

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:50.680
Here. Compare these two.

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:56.340
It's a little sour and harsh.

00:13:56.340 --> 00:13:58.190
It tastes like a lot of 
different things...

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:03.780
This one is bitter, 
but finishes smooth.

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:06.090
Which one do you like Masaki?

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:08.650
I like the one that finished smooth.

00:14:09.140 --> 00:14:10.700
That would be the darker roast.

00:14:11.180 --> 00:14:13.680
The first was the light roast.

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:16.800
You see? It wasn't roasted as long...

00:14:16.800 --> 00:14:17.920
...so the bean is brown.

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:20.110
Exactly. And the bean that's been

00:14:20.110 --> 00:14:22.210
roasted longer is dark like ink.

00:14:22.680 --> 00:14:24.300
So the levels of roasting are determined

00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:26.260
by how burnt the beans are...

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:28.390
Most of the coffee compounds are

00:14:28.390 --> 00:14:30.720
gone in the darker roast that you liked,

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:32.220
so it produces a simpler taste.

00:14:32.460 --> 00:14:34.490
I recommend it to coffee beginners.

00:14:34.750 --> 00:14:42.940
Bean is brown
Light Roast
(Sour and harsh)

00:14:34.750 --> 00:14:42.940
*Recommended 
for 
beginners

00:14:34.750 --> 00:14:42.940
Bean is black
Dark Roast
(Bitter but finishes smooth)

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:39.560
The caffeine content is lower, too.

00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:41.070
If you drink coffee at night,

00:14:41.070 --> 00:14:42.940
it's better to drink a darker roast.

00:14:43.280 --> 00:14:45.210
How unexpected.

00:14:45.210 --> 00:14:47.230
You'd think the darker 
roast would be stronger.

00:14:49.250 --> 00:14:52.050
What kind of coffee do 
you prefer, Master?

00:14:52.800 --> 00:14:55.020
I prefer Jacu coffee.

00:14:55.020 --> 00:14:56.570
Jacu...

00:14:57.200 --> 00:14:58.540
Oh, that bird!

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:01.820
Does he have something 
to do with coffee?

00:15:01.820 --> 00:15:02.910
Yes, he does.

00:15:02.910 --> 00:15:05.210
Jacu coffee is...

00:15:05.780 --> 00:15:07.590
...the coffee beans 
collected from Mr. Jacu

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:09.580
after he's eaten a fully ripened

00:15:09.580 --> 00:15:12.300
coffee cherry and excretes it.

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:13.970
What?!

00:15:14.190 --> 00:15:16.800
That's supposed to be delicious?!

00:15:16.800 --> 00:15:18.970
It is quite delicious.

00:15:18.970 --> 00:15:22.050
A hundred grams costs 
more than 4,000 yen.

00:15:22.050 --> 00:15:23.980
Seriously?! Why?!

00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:26.030
It's expensive because it's rare.

00:15:26.880 --> 00:15:28.620
Similarly, there are coffee beans

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:31.000
collected from the Asian Palm Civet 
after it's eaten the coffee cherry.

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:33.210
That would be kopi luwak.

00:15:33.210 --> 00:15:35.030
Coffee is deep, man!

00:15:35.460 --> 00:15:36.510
It is.

00:15:36.510 --> 00:15:39.890
You still have much to learn.

00:15:39.890 --> 00:15:42.190
We'll teach you a lot more,

00:15:42.190 --> 00:15:44.660
so make sure you review everything 
you've already learned.

00:15:44.660 --> 00:15:46.130
Got it!

00:15:46.630 --> 00:15:48.610
Oh, but wouldn't it be

00:15:48.610 --> 00:15:52.340
good money if you all ate 
the coffee cherries then?

00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:01.380
It never crossed my mind!

00:16:01.380 --> 00:16:03.650
You're quite clever, Masaki!

00:16:04.040 --> 00:16:06.450
Er, I was kidding...

00:16:06.450 --> 00:16:08.050
Keep eating!

00:16:08.050 --> 00:16:09.510
Keep excreting them!

00:16:09.510 --> 00:16:11.600
We'll make a fortune! Come on!

00:16:11.600 --> 00:16:12.370
Um...

00:16:13.650 --> 00:16:16.470
I'd prefer that you 
don't eat the beans.

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:21.080
Currently producing 
beans that cost 
4000 yen per 100g.

00:16:21.100 --> 00:16:26.900
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:24.890
Animal Field Baseball Part 2!

00:16:27.020 --> 00:16:31.590
Continuing From Part 1!

00:16:27.020 --> 00:16:31.590
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:16:35.020 --> 00:16:36.300
What?

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:37.810
A called shot?

00:16:39.360 --> 00:16:42.020
I promised Ichiro.

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:44.040
Ichiro?

00:16:44.540 --> 00:16:45.730
I wonder who that is.

00:16:46.220 --> 00:16:50.340
Ichiro is in the hospital with 
an incurable disease.

00:16:51.060 --> 00:16:56.450
Ichiro said, "Please 
hit a home run for me.

00:16:57.040 --> 00:17:00.920
I can only count on you, Polar Bear,

00:17:00.920 --> 00:17:02.730
the professional baseball player."

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:05.540
It's starting again...

00:17:06.450 --> 00:17:10.500
And as promised, 
I just now hit a home run.

00:17:11.730 --> 00:17:14.770
Just now? I wonder if that's a premonition?

00:17:15.340 --> 00:17:18.440
Emboldened by my home run,

00:17:18.440 --> 00:17:21.510
Ichiro would go on to 
win at Koushien.

00:17:22.480 --> 00:17:24.980
I thought he had an incurable disease?

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:30.040
And currently, he's a star 
in Major League Baseball.

00:17:30.870 --> 00:17:32.900
All right, all right.

00:17:32.900 --> 00:17:35.840
Let's get a move on and continue the game.

00:17:36.260 --> 00:17:39.760
Episode 2: My Promise with Dar.

00:17:40.890 --> 00:17:42.410
The end!

00:17:45.800 --> 00:17:48.260
What a great story.

00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:52.160
Is he trying to get to us mentally?

00:17:52.160 --> 00:17:54.220
He thinks he's clever.

00:17:54.800 --> 00:17:58.000
Thank goodness, Ichiro...

00:18:00.950 --> 00:18:06.140
Polar Bear, you're the Shakespeare 
of the 21st century!

00:18:06.780 --> 00:18:08.540
However,

00:18:08.540 --> 00:18:11.330
baseball is a drama without a set plot!

00:18:11.330 --> 00:18:16.090
Things won't go as you planned!

00:18:17.230 --> 00:18:19.490
Just try and hit it!

00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:24.500
Strike!

00:18:26.670 --> 00:18:28.310
Great job, Boss!

00:18:28.310 --> 00:18:29.920
You're awesome!

00:18:30.950 --> 00:18:32.250
How's that?

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:35.380
Not bad, Grizzly.

00:18:35.820 --> 00:18:39.300
And I'm going to strike you out!

00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:45.120
Reserved

00:18:43.570 --> 00:18:45.770
Cheers!

00:18:55.970 --> 00:18:59.370
Victory beers sure are something else!

00:18:59.370 --> 00:19:01.910
The victory bamboo grass 
is delicious, too.

00:19:02.480 --> 00:19:04.830
So is the victory grass.

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:06.270
You're still eating?

00:19:07.450 --> 00:19:09.750
I always have room for the 
grass at Polar Bear's Café.

00:19:10.250 --> 00:19:12.230
The pasta's pretty good.

00:19:12.230 --> 00:19:14.340
The salmon's not bad, either.

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:22.800
Another!

00:19:22.800 --> 00:19:23.640
Coming right up!

00:19:24.370 --> 00:19:26.600
Damn it. I'm gonna burn it up!

00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:28.600
I'm gonna drink my heart out today!

00:19:29.310 --> 00:19:32.700
It's rather childish of 
you to get all fired up

00:19:32.700 --> 00:19:33.940
over losing a field baseball game.

00:19:34.380 --> 00:19:36.970
You're the one who's childish!

00:19:36.970 --> 00:19:37.900
Why's that?

00:19:37.900 --> 00:19:39.890
What do you mean, "why"?!

00:19:39.890 --> 00:19:41.860
Look how you won the game!

00:19:43.570 --> 00:19:45.530
Just try and hit it!

00:19:45.530 --> 00:19:46.380
Time out!

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:51.120
We're changing batters.

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:55.510
Pinch hitter: Mama Red Squirrel!

00:19:55.510 --> 00:19:57.550
Huh? Me?

00:19:58.300 --> 00:20:02.410
Heavy... This is heavy! H-Heavy!

00:20:03.360 --> 00:20:05.200
Mama Red Squirrel!

00:20:06.710 --> 00:20:08.020
What the hell, Polar Bear?

00:20:08.020 --> 00:20:09.440
Are you throwing the game?

00:20:09.440 --> 00:20:12.100
There's no way someone so 
tiny can hit the ball!

00:20:13.510 --> 00:20:14.510
Ball!

00:20:14.670 --> 00:20:15.940
Strike 
Zone

00:20:16.170 --> 00:20:17.920
Damn it.

00:20:20.300 --> 00:20:20.990
Ball!

00:20:22.490 --> 00:20:23.070
Ball!

00:20:24.690 --> 00:20:26.860
Ball! Four balls!

00:20:26.860 --> 00:20:28.040
Damn it!

00:20:28.520 --> 00:20:31.580
Awesome! That walk scored 
us another run!

00:20:28.990 --> 00:20:31.580
Wow, that's amazing!

00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:35.100
Her strike zone is too small.

00:20:35.720 --> 00:20:38.420
But that won't happen again.

00:20:39.400 --> 00:20:42.130
Pinch-hitter: Mother Red Squirrel.

00:20:42.730 --> 00:20:43.710
What?!

00:20:48.010 --> 00:20:49.390
I'll get it this time...

00:20:50.420 --> 00:20:53.380
Pinch-hitter: Momma Red Squirrel.

00:20:55.170 --> 00:20:56.270
Four balls!

00:20:58.560 --> 00:21:01.360
Pinch-hitter: Mum Red Squirrel.

00:21:01.870 --> 00:21:04.950
Polar Bear!

00:21:11.270 --> 00:21:13.250
Ball! Four balls!

00:21:14.900 --> 00:21:16.460
Yay!

00:21:18.140 --> 00:21:20.050
That's game!

00:21:21.230 --> 00:21:24.000
Your plan was underhanded!

00:21:24.000 --> 00:21:26.400
You mean a clever plan.

00:21:26.400 --> 00:21:27.840
Damn it!

00:21:30.560 --> 00:21:32.270
That ass...

00:21:32.270 --> 00:21:34.480
Now, now. Here's another.

00:21:34.860 --> 00:21:36.150
Boss.

00:21:36.150 --> 00:21:37.810
Cool down, cool down.

00:21:38.060 --> 00:21:40.620
There are no sides after 
the game is done.

00:21:40.620 --> 00:21:42.650
It was so much fun!

00:21:43.690 --> 00:21:46.410
Let's play again sometime, Grizzly.

00:21:48.070 --> 00:21:50.940
Next time, the game will be ours.

00:21:50.940 --> 00:21:52.330
You better be prepared!

00:21:54.050 --> 00:21:55.790
I'll look forward to it.

00:21:57.520 --> 00:22:01.840
I'm... here...

00:22:02.580 --> 00:22:05.730
Play... ball...

00:22:06.450 --> 00:22:13.130
Let's hurry... and start...

00:22:15.410 --> 00:22:24.900
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:23:54.910 --> 00:24:24.990
Next Time

00:23:58.010 --> 00:23:59.700
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:59.700 --> 00:24:00.960
What is it, Panda?

00:24:00.960 --> 00:24:04.520
What's that silver thing you 
put curry into called again?

00:24:04.520 --> 00:24:05.890
Does it actually have a name?

00:24:05.890 --> 00:24:07.330
All right, next question.

00:24:07.330 --> 00:24:09.510
Now I'm curious, tell me.

00:24:09.510 --> 00:24:12.210
I think you should go back 
to your parents' house.

00:24:12.210 --> 00:24:14.760
I'm not asking you how 
I should live my life.

00:24:14.760 --> 00:24:16.260
Let's end this, Polar Bear.

00:24:16.260 --> 00:24:18.280
Next week's Polar Bear's Café

00:24:18.280 --> 00:24:20.020
will be presented to 
you in Morse code.

00:24:20.020 --> 00:24:21.640
I don't think they'd get it.

00:24:21.640 --> 00:24:22.690
Let's just present it normally.

00:24:21.940 --> 00:24:24.560
Panda's Apology
Rin Rin Gets Invited

00:24:22.690 --> 00:24:24.100
Enjoy!
